WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:04.762
- I am 23 years old, I'm Indian,

00:00:05.954 --> 00:00:10.785
and this is the first time
I'm ever gonna go to India,

00:00:11.957 --> 00:00:14.982
and I'm doing it to bring

00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:19.259
my grandfather's ashes back.

00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:24.019
(deep synth music)

00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:27.252
- It's a little bit hard to process.

00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:29.853
When I'd left I was 10,

00:00:29.853 --> 00:00:32.433
and I remember getting on the plane

00:00:32.433 --> 00:00:36.090
and sitting in the
middle of the Pan Am jet,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.240
and I just remember not being able

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.678
to go to sleep because it was so exciting,

00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:43.283
and I kinda feel the same way now.

00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:44.847
- We've made it.

00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:47.448
It's just been really humbling.

00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:51.064
This was the life that I could've had.

00:00:51.064 --> 00:00:55.473
My grandparents left all
of this to come to America.

00:00:55.473 --> 00:00:58.724
- This is clarified butter, and it's added

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:03.336
to the dahl to make it
more savory and delicious.

00:01:03.336 --> 00:01:05.307
- It's very good, you've
gotta have it in it.

00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:06.445
You've got to have it with...

00:01:06.445 --> 00:01:10.138
(mumbling)

00:01:14.846 --> 00:01:16.207
- It's so good.

00:01:16.207 --> 00:01:18.279
- After about a year of
just speaking English

00:01:18.279 --> 00:01:20.819
at the house all the
time, I remember one day

00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:24.994
in my brain all of my
dreams were in Hindi,

00:01:24.994 --> 00:01:27.269
and then one day they turned into English.

00:01:27.269 --> 00:01:29.362
- There's just something about being here

00:01:29.362 --> 00:01:33.913
and having access to
like the country's spices

00:01:33.913 --> 00:01:35.904
that makes it completely different.

00:01:35.904 --> 00:01:37.976
- We are going to see the homes

00:01:37.976 --> 00:01:40.536
where (mumbles) grew up.

00:01:40.536 --> 00:01:41.776
- [Voiceover] How are you feeling

00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:44.234
about going back to see your house?

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.535
- [Voiceover] I'm very excited,

00:01:45.535 --> 00:01:48.095
and I'm gonna take a lot of pictures.

00:01:48.095 --> 00:01:49.679
- [Voiceover] So, where's the house dad?

00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:51.142
- It should be at the end.

00:01:51.142 --> 00:01:51.935
- [Voiceover] It's in the...

00:01:51.935 --> 00:01:53.052
- Yeah, it should be down here.

00:01:53.052 --> 00:01:57.983
This is the balcony
where we used to stand,

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:01.179
mommy and I, and watch
everybody play soccer.

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:04.044
I just remember walking,

00:02:04.044 --> 00:02:07.315
walking with my grandmother to get milk.

00:02:07.315 --> 00:02:09.042
We would go at four in the morning.

00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:12.557
After we came back, we
would meditate and pray,

00:02:12.557 --> 00:02:15.361
and that was a daily
routine, seven days a week.

00:02:15.361 --> 00:02:16.478
- [Voiceover] What do you think,

00:02:16.478 --> 00:02:19.079
looking at this house,
about what it's like

00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:20.760
to live in America now?

00:02:26.362 --> 00:02:28.861
- I don't think there's
any way to compare the two.

00:02:28.861 --> 00:02:32.457
So, on the roof upstairs,
we used to get up there,

00:02:32.457 --> 00:02:35.159
and we would fly kites,
and we would have contests

00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:37.862
with neighbors to see
who could use the string

00:02:37.862 --> 00:02:39.609
to cut down a neighbor's kite,

00:02:39.609 --> 00:02:41.417
and those were called kite fights.

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:45.490
Smaller kids played cricket
in this part of the park,

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.517
and then the larger kids
played cricket in this park.

00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:52.804
There used to be a bush, and
I jumped in the bush one day,

00:02:52.804 --> 00:02:55.160
and inside the bush was a bees' nest,

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.741
and I started screaming
(speaking in Hindi)

00:02:57.741 --> 00:02:59.096
which means I'm dying.

00:03:00.005 --> 00:03:02.019
- Seeing everything has made me

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:04.962
just so much more thankful and grateful

00:03:04.962 --> 00:03:09.908
for my grandfather and
everything that he did.

00:03:09.908 --> 00:03:12.306
There are so many things
that happen in the city

00:03:12.306 --> 00:03:16.926
that it's really overwhelming
for like my stimulus.

00:03:16.926 --> 00:03:17.992
Yeah.

00:03:17.992 --> 00:03:20.998
I think know now like where I get

00:03:20.998 --> 00:03:24.980
my hustle from because
this city does not stop.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.535
Tomorrow, we are going to Haridwar

00:03:28.535 --> 00:03:30.771
to the river Ganges to deposit

00:03:30.771 --> 00:03:33.147
my grandfather's ashes into the river

00:03:33.147 --> 00:03:36.820
and I think that's gonna
be like pretty intense.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.695
I am so thankful that I can be here

00:03:40.695 --> 00:03:42.848
to honor my grandfather that way.

00:03:42.848 --> 00:03:45.123
I already feel like I'm changed

00:03:45.123 --> 00:03:47.319
after just one day.

00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:51.937
(acoustic music)

